{"repositoryId":1304712385,"availability":"available","full":"harishkotra/kairo","name":"kairo","description":"Kairo — observability for multi-agent mobile software engineering","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":8,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-18T07:51:31Z","updated":"2026-07-21T19:29:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kairo-woad-nu.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://kairo-woad-nu.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:25.203Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:25.203Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:25.203Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T18:04:25.203Z","stars":8,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Observability for multi-agent mobile software engineering.","Kairo is a collaborative workspace where specialized agents design and ship an Expo mobile app from a product brief, while every step stays inspectable: agents, VMs, events, artifacts, decisions, memory, metrics, live device previews, and backend traces.","Describe the product. Agents plan screens, run in isolation, and compose a shared design system. You watch the build unfold on a Figma-like canvas, scrub time-travel replay, scan Expo Go QR when the primary screen ships, and export telemetry to Laminar without leaving Kairo as the control surface."],"features":["Free-text product brief","Curated example library (focus timer, recipes, habits, markets, budget, studio booking, trips, standups)","Planner (mock heuristics or live LLM) returns navigation + 2–5 screens - not a fixed Home/Profile/Settings shell","Architecture - routes & navigation from the brief","Design system - dual-theme tokens + shared primitives"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/harishkotra/kairo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eb5c3e311908e66abbfae1ae1ad56130f91acb467f7594df2c810de82b08fdf6","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:25.495Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:25.495Z","projectInsights":{"version